  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Aspafilioside C and the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, as it is indirectly linked through multiple targets. Aspafilioside C is predicted to act as a target for Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by Diplotrin A and Palmyramide A. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of the 26S proteasome, a key component of the proteasome complex responsible for protein degradation. The shared pathway from Aspafilioside C to Caspase-5 and then to the proteasome subunit indicates a possible mechanism by which Aspafilioside C may influence proteasome activity. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain. The evidence supports a plausible pathway, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction and functional role of Aspafilioside C in this process.",
